@* A disabled button fires no pointer events, so a tooltip on it never opens — which is the one
   moment a reader most needs to be told why it is disabled. Wrap it: the span takes the hover,
   the button stays disabled, and the reason is announced because the wrapper is focusable and
   describes it. *@
<div class="flex items-center gap-3">
    <span tabindex="0" data-slot="tooltip-trigger" data-target="tip-why"
          aria-describedby="tip-why" class="inline-flex rounded-md">
        <Button disabled>Publish</Button>
    </span>
    <TooltipContent Id="tip-why">Add a payment method first.</TooltipContent>
</div>
